{
  "_comment": "Ground truth for the greengate secret-detection benchmark. Positives are lines that ANY competent secret scanner should flag. Negatives are FP-trap files: high-entropy-but-harmless strings, placeholders, public/test keys, and documented example values. Any finding a tool reports that does not match a positive (file,line) is counted as a false positive. All secret VALUES are synthetic and non-functional.",
  "_secrets_note": "To keep contiguous provider-format secrets out of the repository (and out of GitHub secret-scanning / push-protection), fixture files ship with a __GG_SECRET__ placeholder and the real synthetic value is base64-encoded in `secret_b64`. run.py materializes the corpus into a temp dir, substituting the decoded value on the same line, before any tool scans it. Line numbers are preserved.",
  "line_tolerance": 2,
  "placeholder": "__GG_SECRET__",
